messages:
sam: Hey team — after upgrading to redwood-js-sdk v1.3.2 our edge functions on Vercel are intermittently hanging when consuming ReadableStream from the SDK. Repro below. Happens only when token rotation is enabled and there are backpressure pauses. Anyone seen this?

support-bot: Acknowledged. Filed INC-4382, pinging @eng-runtime. Can you paste a minimal repro + Node/runtime details?

sam: Minimal repro (Node edge runtime, Node 20, Vercel Edge):
```js
const res = await client.stream({ model: 'gpt-small', input: 'ping' });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  console.log('chunk', new TextDecoder().decode(value));
  // simulate backpressure
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200));
}
```
Auth: token rotation via async refreshToken() invoked by SDK (rotate every 5s). SDK pinned to 1.3.2. Logs show a 401 just before the hang.

maria: Have you tried downgrading to 1.2.7? We've seen similar streaming fixes in that range.

sam: I tried 1.2.7 — hang disappears. 1.3.1/1.3.2 reproduce reliably under load. Also see repeated `WARN auth: refresh failed 401` in proxy logs immediately before the stream stops delivering chunks.

alex: Looks like the in-flight token-rotation + retry path may be aborting the underlying reader. @eng-runtime can you check the PR that changed retry-on-401 behavior in 1.3.x? :eyes:

devx: Quick workaround: disable automatic token rotation or pass a static bearer token in headers: `client.stream({ headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${staticToken}` } })` — that seems to avoid the hang.

support-bot: Can you share a short HAR or curl reproduction? Also try `retry: { maxRetries: 0 }` to see if skipping retries changes behaviour.

sam: Gist with tiny repro + logs: https://gist.github.com/example/repro-stream-rot — logs show: `WARN auth: refresh failed 401 -> scheduling retry`, then silence from the stream. first_message_ts=2141594321

julie: I can repro locally with edge emulation. When the SDK refreshes a token while the stream has an active reader, we trigger a retry flow that re-fetches with the new token but the underlying ReadableStream becomes locked and subsequent `reader.read()` never resolves. Hypothesis: abort controller signal or stream piping is lost during retry.

julie: Temporary mitigations: set env `REDWOOD_STREAM_RETRY=disabled` to opt-out of in-flight retries for streams, or pin to `redwood-js-sdk@1.2.7`. We will ship a patch in 1.3.3 to preserve stream reader state across token refresh. Escalating for hotfix. :shipit:

sam: Thanks — that matches our test. ETA for 1.3.3?

julie: ETA tomorrow EOD PST for a hotfix release and staging deploy. We'll post release notes + migration steps.

sam: Applied `REDWOOD_STREAM_RETRY=disabled` and confirmed the hang is gone. Thanks everyone :raised_hands:
